From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:23:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 151/151] Find: In selection is a ticked box over the current
 selection, as in Notepad++

"In selection" kept the range it was turned on with and followed it through
replaces, so after Replace all and a click that dropped the selection, the
box still showed ticked and the count reported "No results" for the old
range while Find next found matches elsewhere.

As in Notepad++, the box is now only a ticked flag, enabled while the
active tab has a selection (not empty, not a column block). Replace all,
the count and the highlights take the selection at that moment when the
box is ticked and enabled, else the whole text. Without a selection the
box shows its ticked state disabled. After Replace all in a selection the
replaced range stays selected. The flag ends with the find bar; a
selection of 1024 characters or more still ticks it when the bar opens.

Removes the stored range (tab, positions, text generation), its refresh
and follow-the-edit code (find_range::scope's old form, find_range::edited).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

